  "notes": [
    "Generated by: cargo run --release --locked -p nana-ui-runtime --features benchmark --bin nana-theme-benchmark -- --output target/performance/issue101/theme.json",
    "Issue #101 \u00a74 baseline. work counts are the contract; elapsed_ms is a host observation.",
    "Controls are product Buttons through AppContext, not bare divs: a Button is what carries SemanticPaint and InteractionStyle.",
    "work counts are identical across the 4 runs folded here and are reproducible; elapsed_ms is the per-case minimum of those runs. Do not read elapsed_ms across recordings as a regression signal: the same binary on this host ranged nearly 2x on theme-head-style-mutation depending on what else was building. Compare timings only A/B within one sitting.",
    "layout_copies / layout_copied_bytes are new in this recording: the LayoutStyle a style write copies to hold a node resolved design intent beside the layout it authored. A metrics change pays one copy per control that has intent; a palette or accent change must pay none, which theme-palette-switch and theme-accent-only now assert as required invariants."
